[block'ORD-0040-order-coherence'
  [ref'EMS']
  [ctx'the spec of EMS-002','.guidelines/.orders/EMS-002/EMS-002.pgml']
  [ctx'the ratified steps, the measured proposal and the answers of the Regent','.guidelines/.orders/INTAKE-ORDER-COHERENCE.md, sections 4, 5, 9, 10 and 11']
  [ctx'the configuration of a series, which the claim hands the check to','.guidelines/.orders/EMS-002/ORD-0039']
  [tgt'step 3 of the trail to the final Explorer, in the Rust only: an Order says where it stands, the Rust reads the claim from its AST, writes it into the manifest as relates, refuses to bundle a claim that does not match, and checks every Order bundled from this one on']
  [ins'read the claim from the AST, as binds and ref are read: a reference to EMS, to nem, or to an ORD-#### of its own directory, bare or under override, instead-of, deprecated, derive-from or see-also, the relation command naming the kind and its own literals the reason']
  [ins'have the Rust --bundle write relates, one order, kind and reason per claim, and refuse with nothing written when a claim does not match its destination']
  [ins'add glyph --check, which reads every bundle under a folder, holds the Orders bundled from this one on, and answers fix for a mismatch and ask for an Order that makes no claim']
  [ins'run glyph --check over .guidelines/.orders in npm run check']
  [cnst'the trigger is mismatch, not absence: an Order with no claim is asked, never refused']
  [cnst'the closed Orders are read as emitted, and nothing is asked of them']
  [cnst'the JS neither extracts relates nor runs the check, and every run of the command line oracle still answers the same bytes in both engines']
  [cnst'no hash of the snapshot moves; no crate enters']
  [cnst'npm run check and npm run check:rust green']
  [val'the rules','each mismatch, the absent claim and the cycle of supersession seen refused or asked by a test that failed before the code it holds']
];
